WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.501
The visit with the Chesters was even shorter than the one with the Tudors.

2
00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:12.366
Jo and the boys erupted in laughing fits several more times before Amy made her excuses to leave.

3
00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:20.037
"Are you leaving already? The boys seem to be having so much fun with your sister," Mary remarked slyly.

4
00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:26.889
"Jo has a natural way with children," replied Amy in a composed voice, but feeling ashamed.

5
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:32.831
"We would love to stay, but I’m afraid our next appointment will require a little more traveling time."

6
00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:40.345
"Of course, I forgot that you don’t have a carriage," Mary said innocently, but with a stab in her sentence.

7
00:00:40.346 --> 00:00:47.080
Smiling sweetly, Amy thanked Mrs. Chester and Mary for their hospitality then called out to Jo.

8
00:00:47.081 --> 00:00:56.387
As soon as the door of the Chester home had closed, Amy’s frozen smile melted, and she turned to Jo in anger.

9
00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:59.420
"Can’t you behave like a lady just for once?

10
00:00:59.421 --> 00:01:06.492
Why do you choose to make a fool of yourself, of me, of our family?" she practically yelled in the middle of the street.

11
00:01:06.493 --> 00:01:11.355
"Lower your voice, dear, people are watching," Jo said mockingly.

12
00:01:11.356 --> 00:01:17.858
"Jo! I’m serious! Why are you determined to ruin my life?" Amy cried passionately.

13
00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:23.441
"Why should I pretend to be something I’m not?" retorted Jo, who was close to shouting too.

14
00:01:23.442 --> 00:01:27.828
"I really don’t like these people nor am I interested in their lives!"

15
00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:36.415
Regaining her composure, Amy breathed deeply and said, "Because that’s how people will learn to respect us and treat us better."

16
00:01:36.416 --> 00:01:40.527
Shaking her head, Jo said, "You’re wrong, Amy.

17
00:01:40.528 --> 00:01:44.919
No matter how nice we are to them, they won’t think of us as their equal.

18
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:48.020
I thought you realized that after your party."

19
00:01:48.021 --> 00:01:51.910
The two sisters walked in silence for a while, then Amy spoke up.

20
00:01:51.911 --> 00:02:00.078
"Maybe you’re right, but I still believe that good will come if we try to show kindness to others regardless of how they see us."

21
00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:05.870
"That’s why you are a dreamer, Amy," acknowledged Jo, "and I love you for it.

22
00:02:05.871 --> 00:02:13.410
But me? I’m practical and realistic and I don’t believe that I have to change just to make another person happy."

23
00:02:13.411 --> 00:02:16.490
"Then I won’t ask you to," Amy said.

24
00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:20.125
"You are you, Jo, and I love you for it too."

25
00:02:20.126 --> 00:02:25.157
Stopping in front of Aunt March’s house, the two sisters gave each other a quick hug.

26
00:02:25.158 --> 00:02:28.332
"Can I be me now?" Jo asked playfully.

27
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:35.458
"Of course," smiled Amy. "Besides, Aunt March knows your true colors anyway."

28
00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:41.929
Giggling, the sisters held hands as they walked up toward the large mansion.

29
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:46.870
Aunt March’s housemaid Esther brought the girls to the west wing sitting room.

30
00:02:46.871 --> 00:02:54.664
(Aunt March’s mansion was so gigantic that she had three sitting rooms, one in each direction except for east.)

31
00:02:54.665 --> 00:03:02.811
The old lady sat in her "throne," as Jo called her large velvet armchair with gold armrests and satin cushions.

32
00:03:02.812 --> 00:03:10.319
Aunt March was feeding crackers to Polly who, upon seeing them, screeched loudly, "Mind your mouth!"

33
00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:16.229
"Hello, Aunt March," said Amy, walking over and kissing her on both cheeks.

34
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:23.351
Jo stood awkwardly because in all the years she had come to work at this house, she had never greeted her aunt with a kiss.

35
00:03:23.352 --> 00:03:31.712
"What are you standing there for like a stone statue?" the old lady snapped at Jo. "Polly needs more crackers."

36
00:03:31.713 --> 00:03:34.174
"Crackers!" screeched the parrot.

37
00:03:34.175 --> 00:03:39.947
Without another word, Jo turned around and headed toward the kitchen to do as Aunt March told her.

38
00:03:39.948 --> 00:03:46.276
When she returned with the crackers and a dish of clean water for the bird, Jo saw a rare sight:

39
00:03:46.277 --> 00:03:53.038
the deep lines on her aunt’s face had softened and the corners of her mouth lifted upward in a smile. "Now

40
00:03:53.039 --> 00:03:58.049
Aunt March, I insist that you let me adjust these pillows back here. You

41
00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:04.785
don’t look very comfortable sitting there," said Amy, carefully rearranging the cushions on Aunt March’s chair. "I’m

42
00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:11.271
fine," Aunt March said in a much more tender voice than she had ever used with Jo. "Where

43
00:04:11.272 --> 00:04:18.949
is that sister of yours? Has she gone to make her own crackers? Polly is starving here." "Here

44
00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:25.193
we go," said Jo in an overly cheery voice, as she pushed the crackers into Polly’s face. "Let

45
00:04:25.194 --> 00:04:32.538
me do it, Jo," Amy said, taking the dish from her and expertly breaking off pieces to feed the bird. Jo

46
00:04:32.539 --> 00:04:36.520
had to admit that Amy excelled at her job. Even

47
00:04:36.521 --> 00:04:43.377
though Jo knew Amy was not fond of the bird, at that moment, you could not see Amy’s true feelings, because

48
00:04:43.378 --> 00:04:47.060
she treated Polly as gently as Aunt March did. When

49
00:04:47.061 --> 00:04:50.098
Esther brought in the tea and biscuits, Jo

50
00:04:50.099 --> 00:04:57.612
wandered over to the bookshelves to see if Aunt March had gotten any new books since she stopped working for her. "Josephine,

51
00:04:57.613 --> 00:05:02.868
I’d like to hear a story," Aunt March called to her. "Amy

52
00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:08.318
here is a darling, but no one can read a story like you can, dear." Feeling

53
00:05:08.319 --> 00:05:15.026
touched, Jo selected a new book that she thought would be interesting and took it over to Aunt March. "No.

54
00:05:15.027 --> 00:05:21.432
That one’s terribly boring. Bring Stories from the Garden ," said her aunt.

55
00:05:21.433 --> 00:05:25.956
"But doesn’t The Pirate’s Treasure Box sound more exciting and adventurous?"

56
00:05:25.957 --> 00:05:30.767
Jo asked persuasively, since the title was especially appealing to her.

57
00:05:30.768 --> 00:05:36.635
"I don’t care for that one, Josephine. The other one is better," Aunt March said firmly.

58
00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:43.356
"Yes, Aunt March," Jo said, bringing the garden stories book and sitting down next to her aunt.

59
00:05:43.357 --> 00:05:48.967
Amy poured the tea and chose some biscuits for Aunt March while Jo opened the book to read.

60
00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:52.810
"Girls, there is something I want to discuss with you,"

61
00:05:52.811 --> 00:06:00.882
Aunt March began as she accepted the teacup from Amy with one hand, while placing the other on Jo’s arm to stop her from reading.

62
00:06:00.883 --> 00:06:05.375
The sisters looked at her expectantly, waiting for her to continue.

63
00:06:05.376 --> 00:06:10.857
"As you know, every summer I travel to Europe for a holiday," said Aunt March.

64
00:06:10.858 --> 00:06:21.004
"This year I have chosen to spend the entire year abroad as my health has worsened and the warmer climates seem to improve it somewhat."

65
00:06:21.005 --> 00:06:25.874
"Of course, Aunt March, your health is the main priority," said Amy.

66
00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:33.276
Nodding at her, Aunt March continued. "However, the doctor recommends that I travel with a companion . . ."

67
00:06:33.277 --> 00:06:38.984
Aunt March chose to pause here, sip her tea, and adjust a cushion before continuing.

68
00:06:38.985 --> 00:06:44.892
Meanwhile, both Jo and Amy, realizing what Aunt March was about to announce, held their breath.

69
00:06:44.893 --> 00:06:50.829
Each girl hoped her heart wouldn’t jump out of her chest because it was beating so fast.

70
00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:56.098
"I must confess it was a hard decision for me to make," said Aunt March.

71
00:06:56.099 --> 00:07:03.072
"Whether you believe it or not, I am fond of both of you for obviously different reasons.

72
00:07:03.073 --> 00:07:13.144
However, as I will be covering all expenses for this trip, I expect my companion to be someone who will do exactly as I say."

73
00:07:13.145 --> 00:07:20.628
Jo could hardly sit still since her dream of traveling to Europe seemed about to come true in the next few seconds.

74
00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:31.003
Then looking at each girl long and hard, Aunt March held out her hand and said, "Therefore, I’ve decided to take Amy to Europe with me."

